Decision rules:
- Choose a candidate only if a student who mastered the old objective would be
  assessed on substantially the same skill by the new one. Sharing a topic area is
  not enough — "calculating averages" and "drawing bar charts" are both statistics
  and are NOT the same objective.
- A difference in grade level or in how demanding the wording is does not disqualify
  a candidate, provided the underlying skill matches.
- Prefer declining over a loose match. A wrong binding silently mis-targets every one
  of these {{ question_count }} questions, and nothing downstream will detect it.
  Declining simply routes them to a human, which is cheap by comparison.

Respond with ONLY a JSON object, no prose and no code fences:
{"choice": <candidate number, or null if none is a genuine match>, "confidence": <"high"|"medium"|"low">, "reason": "<one short sentence>"}
